# TEST-ONLY aius-ota Ed25519 SECRET key (64 bytes, hex: 32-byte seed then
# 32-byte public key).
#
# NOT A SECRET, AND DELIBERATELY SO. Its seed is the ASCII string
# "aius-ota-test-only-key-notsecret", published in this file and in the
# regeneration command below, so anyone can reproduce it. It exists to give the
# host suites a real Ed25519 keypair to sign and verify with; it must never sign
# a firmware image anybody installs, and the matching public key must never be
# compiled into a device.
#
# A production secret key is generated by the operator, on a host, and kept off
# the build machine: tools/ota/aius_ota_sign.py --help prints that command.
#
# Regenerate (identical hex line):
#   tools/ota/aius_ota_sign.py keygen \
#       --public test/ota/test-only-signing-key.pub \
#       --secret test/ota/test-only-signing-key.sec \
#       --seed-hex 616975732d6f74612d746573742d6f6e6c792d6b65792d6e6f74736563726574
616975732d6f74612d746573742d6f6e6c792d6b65792d6e6f74736563726574f36fb0b8312403ee37b965b64dce113eca79d401dc684190c2a02caca0604d30
